## 7. Technical architecture for Google AI Studio

I recommend using Google AI Studio to generate the first working version, with a clearly specified frontend architecture and a structured content system. The priority is to get the information architecture and all seven chapters right before spending time on advanced 3D effects.

## Recommended stack

React + TypeScript + Vite

Component-based development, typed content structures, and a fast local development environment.

Tailwind CSS

Consistent typography, spacing, responsive layouts, colors, and reusable design tokens.

Reusable React components

Shared chapter templates, section navigation, evidence panels, source notes, and diagram containers. Use shadcn/ui selectively if its setup works with the generated project.

Recharts + SVG diagrams

Responsive charts and lightweight diagrams. Prefer SVG and CSS animations over heavy 3D scenes where they communicate the same information.

Framer Motion (Motion for React)

Page transitions, subtle reveal effects, chapter transitions, and restrained motion. Keep all essential content available without animation.

Static deployment

Deploy the finished frontend to Vercel or another compatible static host. A database is unnecessary unless you later introduce persistent user features.

